  "name": "Question 2",
  "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+20}{(x+6)^{2}}=\\frac{A}{x+6}+\\frac{2}{(x+6)^{2}},\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $A?$",
  "worked_solution": "Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+6)^{2}$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+20 & =A(x+6)+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLetting $x=0$  gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(0)+20 & =A(0+6)+2 \\\\ 20 & =6A+2 \\\\ 18 & =6A \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
